# ANCHORED, and it matters. This line was `scripts/`, and .semgrepignore uses gitignore semantics: an
# unanchored directory pattern matches a directory of that name at ANY depth. It was written when
# `scripts/` meant the repo-root shell wrappers, and it silently grew to cover apps/web/scripts/,
# packages/asciidoc-pdf/scripts/ and packages/shared/scripts/ — ~6,150 lines of first-party generator
# JavaScript, including build-print-highlight-css.mjs, which composes CSS selectors and comments out
# of external input behind hand-rolled `safeName`/`commentSafe`/`selectorSafeName` guards. Exactly the
# code SAST is for, excluded by a pattern nobody meant to point at it. Measured on semgrep 1.170.0: a
# probe tree with an `eval()` in five `scripts/` directories reported one file under `scripts/` and
# four under it once anchored.
#
# What is excluded now is what the line was written for — the shell wrappers under the root scripts/
# tree. `scripts/ci/architecture-guard.mjs` is first-party JavaScript and is scanned like any other.
/scripts/**/*.sh
